  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Data shows that 68% of Latino adults in the US are interested in the FIFA World Cup 2026™, and 41% are taking a trip related to the tournament that they wouldn't have planned otherwise.*

-  56% are traveling with extended family, and 64% say staying together is essential
-  61% prefer short-term rentals over hotels, with kitchen amenities and gathering spaces making group travel more comfortable and practical
-  67% rate visiting local restaurants and shops as highly important, driving economic impact in host city communities
-  Miami, Los Angeles, and New York/New Jersey are top destinations, where travel and cultural connection go hand in hand

Big events bring people together. But for US Latino families, togetherness is the event. More here → <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/emUVq9_w?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/emUVq9_w</a>

* Study conducted by Blue Point Analytix for Airbnb

<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fbiggestgameonearth&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#BiggestGameOnEarth</a></p>
