  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">The FIFA World Cup 2026™ will generate over $1 billion in local economic impact from Airbnb guests, according to Deloitte. 

But that number doesn’t tell the whole story.

Our $5 million Host City Impact Program is making sure the people who live in these cities share in that growth. Here's what that looks like on the ground:

- 11 new and refurbished soccer mini-pitches across New York, New Jersey, and California
- More than $1 million invested in Houston for green infrastructure and youth soccer access
- Over 3,000 free match tickets donated to youth in underserved communities
- More than $550,000 CAD in soccer infrastructure across 4 Ontario communities
- Free post-match transit for fans after every Philadelphia match via SEPTA's Broad Street Line
- Investments in Kansas City’s Open Doors! small business program and Rhode Island’s Summer of Soccer
- A community-driven exhibition of art and memorabilia celebrating Mexico City’s rich football heritage
- Fan Zone grants to create gathering spaces in 9 communities across Washington state

More coming as the tournament progresses. 

<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fbiggestgameonearth&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#BiggestGameOnEarth</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Ffifaworldcup&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#FIFAWorldCup</a></p>
